---
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';

const page = {
  path: '/technical-seo-services-philippines/',
  title: 'Technical SEO Services Philippines | Bright Forge SEO',
  description: 'Technical SEO from our Philippines team: we find indexing, speed, redirect and rendering faults and give your developer the URLs, the fix and the test.',
  h1: 'Technical SEO Services in the Philippines',
  crumb: 'Technical SEO',
  enquiry: '/contact/?service=technical-seo#contactForm',
  lead: [
    'Technical SEO deals with the faults that stop Google reading a website properly: pages missing from the index, duplicate URLs, slow templates, broken redirects, content hidden behind JavaScript. We find them, explain each one to your developer and confirm the fix once it is live.',
  ],
  secondary: { href: '/samples/technical-review-handoff.csv', label: 'See a sample handoff (CSV)' },
  sections: [
    {
      h2: 'Problems we are usually called in for',
      html: `<ul class="bf-list">
<li>Important pages are not indexed.</li>
<li>Traffic fell after a redesign or a platform change.</li>
<li>The site is slow and fails Core Web Vitals.</li>
<li>Search Console shows errors nobody has had time to examine.</li>
<li>An online shop's filters have created thousands of near-identical URLs.</li>
<li>A relaunch is planned and should not go wrong. See <a href="/website-migration-services/">website migration services</a>.</li>
</ul>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'What we check',
      html: `<p>Crawling and indexing; redirects and canonicals; site structure and internal links; page speed and Core Web Vitals; mobile layout; JavaScript rendering; structured data; XML sitemaps and robots.txt; security and HTTPS.</p>
<p>Two faults we see often are covered in our articles on <a href="/blog/robots-txt-mistakes-that-block-google/">robots.txt mistakes that block Google</a> and <a href="/blog/soft-404s-in-search-console/">soft 404s in Search Console</a>.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'What you receive',
      html: `<p>For each fault, one short brief:</p>
<dl class="bf-deliverables">
<dt>The page and the fault</dt><dd>Affected URLs, with a screenshot or crawl extract.</dd>
<dt>The change</dt><dd>What should be different, written for a developer.</dd>
<dt>The live check</dt><dd>How we will confirm it worked.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Briefs are ordered by effect on search, with the likely effort for each. See a real example: our <a href="/samples/technical-review-handoff.csv">technical review handoff</a>, a review of our own website before repairs, showing findings and acceptance checks.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'How we do it, step by step',
      html: `<ol class="bf-steps">
<li>Crawl the site and gather Search Console, analytics and speed data.</li>
<li>Reproduce each fault, so we report causes and not symptoms.</li>
<li>Prioritise.</li>
<li>Write the briefs, or make the changes ourselves where we have access.</li>
<li>Test after release and record the result.</li>
<li>Monitor monthly on an ongoing programme.</li>
</ol>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Platforms',
      html: `<p>We work with WordPress, Shopify and WooCommerce sites and with sites built on JavaScript frameworks. Our own site is built on Astro. Where a fault needs a rebuild and not a patch, our <a href="/development/">web design and development</a> team can do it.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Pricing',
      html: `<p>We do not publish a rate card. A one-off technical review, or technical work within a monthly programme, is scoped in a written proposal.</p>`,
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { question: 'Do you make the changes or only recommend them?', answer: 'Either. Many clients have a developer; some give us access.' },
    { question: 'Will this improve rankings on its own?', answer: 'It removes obstacles. A site with good content and technical faults often improves quickly once they are fixed; a site with weak content will also need content work.' },
    { question: 'How is this different from an SEO audit?', answer: 'An <a href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit</a> also covers content, keywords and links. This service goes deeper on the technical side and includes checking the fixes.' },
  ],
};
---
<EditorialPage page={page} />
